Method: fr.baretto.ollamassist.agent.tools.files.SourceRootResolver#effectiveSourceRoots
Doc: * Returns effective source roots: configured IntelliJ roots first, falling back to a
     * project-type-aware filesystem scan when none are configured.
     *
     * <p>Works across JetBrains IDEs: IntelliJ, GoLand, WebStorm, PhpStorm, RustRover, etc.
     * Project type is detected from well-known marker files rather than language assumptions.
Signature: private static List<VirtualFile> effectiveSourceRoots(Project project)
Body: {
    ProjectRootManager prm = ProjectRootManager.getInstance(project);
    List<VirtualFile> configured = prm == null ? List.of() : sortByPreference(Arrays.asList(prm.getContentSourceRoots()));
    if (!configured.isEmpty())
        return configured;
    String basePath = project.getBasePath();
    if (basePath == null)
        return List.of();
    // Resolve candidates ordered by preference for the detected project type
    List<String> candidates = sourceCandidatesForProject(basePath);
    if (candidates.isEmpty())
        return List.of();
    List<VirtualFile> found = new ArrayList<>();
    for (String candidate : candidates) {
        if (new File(basePath, candidate).isDirectory()) {
            VirtualFile vf = LocalFileSystem.getInstance().refreshAndFindFileByPath(basePath + "/" + candidate);
            if (vf != null && vf.isValid()) {
                found.add(vf);
                // take the first (highest-priority) match
                break;
            }
        }
    }
    if (!found.isEmpty()) {
        log.debug("SourceRootResolver: filesystem fallback → {}", found);
    }
    return found;
}

